1) One-liner & Value Prop

Spuds is “Eventbrite × Airbnb for gamers”: a place to host or join casual in-person gaming parties nearby. Guests browse local parties by game, platform, skill vibe, party size, and vibe (chill/competitive/co-op); Hosts create a listing with time, address (hidden until RSVP), capacity, rules, required gear, and optional cost-share.

Primary jobs:

Guests: “Find safe, nearby people to play the games I love—tonight or this weekend.”

Hosts: “Fill seats at my gaming night with the right people and ground rules.”

2) Target Users & Constraints

Guests (18+): console/PC/board-game players looking for IRL sessions.

Hosts (18+): people with a living room/garage, café space, or a small venue.

Safety: soft real-name policy (first name + initial), verified email/phone, ratings, report/ban system, address reveals post-RSVP, optional ID check later.

3) MVP Scope (what ships in v1)

Public landing page (SEO-friendly)

Auth (email magic link or OAuth Google/Discord)

Location-aware Discover (city + radius, map/list)

Party Details (title, date/time, tags, host profile, seat count, rules)

Host flow (create/edit/delete parties, see RSVPs, approve/auto-accept)

RSVP flow (request to join or instant join if enabled)

Messaging (host ↔ guest event chat; global DMs can come later)

Ratings + reports after an event

Basic notifications (email + in-app)

Admin panel (remove parties, ban users, view reports)

Nice-to-have next: payments/cost-share, waitlists, calendar sync, group features, photo uploads.

