Landing page (Next.js + Tailwind):

Build a Next.js (App Router) page at / using Tailwind that renders the Spuds hero (H1/Subhead/CTAs), a “How it works” 3-card grid, a “Popular this week” section with placeholder PartyCard components, a Safety/Trust strip, and a footer with links. Use the color tokens in the spec and export a Metadata object for SEO (title/description/OpenGraph). Make the layout responsive and accessible (semantic HTML, aria-labels).

Discover page:

Create /discover with a search bar (city input), radius slider, date quick filters, and chips for game/platform/vibe. Implement a map (Mapbox GL JS) on desktop left, list on right; mobile toggles. Fetch parties from /api/parties with query params; render skeletons while loading.

Party API (Supabase):

Scaffold the Postgres tables from the SQL schema provided. Add RLS policies so users can only edit their own parties and read public fields. Implement Next.js API routes for /api/parties (GET list, POST create), /api/parties/:id (GET detail, PATCH, DELETE), /api/parties/:id/rsvps (POST), and /api/rsvps/:id (PATCH). Validate inputs with Zod.

Auth with magic links:

Add Supabase Auth with email magic link. Create /login page and protect /host/* routes server-side. Store user profile in users table on first login.

Event chat:

Add /api/parties/:id/messages (GET/POST). On Party Detail, render a chat panel that’s only visible to accepted guests/host; use server actions or SWR polling.

Address masking:

In Party Detail API, only include address if the requesting user has an accepted RSVP or is the host; otherwise return address_masked: true.

